  "notes": [
    "Original Sun snv_111b kernel, booted from an installed virtual disk; this is separate from illumos testing.",
    "Network egress is disabled; SSH is forwarded only on localhost.",
    "Tests ran as the ordinary ipctest user.",
    "Development files came from the archived original IPS repository, with each extracted payload checked against its manifest SHA-1 content hash.",
    "GCC 4.3 warns about valid zero-initialized aggregates under -Wextra; only that warning was disabled.",
    "The archived ISO MD5 matches the mirror checksum listing. SHA-256 is a local provenance pin.",
    "Native CMake 3.16.9 was built using bootstrapped GCC 4.8.5, with its existing SUNOS_NO_IFADDRS fallback, OpenSSL disabled, and the saved utimes compatibility patch. The library itself was compiled with original GCC 4.3.2.",
    "pkg-config 0.29.2 was built using GCC 4.3.2 with -march=i686 and the saved GLib locale-header ordering patch.",
    "Original pkg-config 0.23 passes normal-prefix shared/static consumers. It truncates paths containing spaces.",
    "CMake 3.16 FindPkgConfig also splits escaped spaces. Relocated pkg-config consumers therefore use Python 2.4 shlex to pass the emitted flags directly to the native compiler. Separate relocated consumers exercise the CMake exports.",
    "Source hashes identify the tested checkout; coverage is limited to the C and packaging scopes stated above."
  ],
